+# hvir
+
+hvir is a cross-platform desktop workbench for developers who live in the terminal.
+It combines fast embedded terminals, git worktree workflows, remote SSH
+workspaces, a rich file and document viewer, and first-class integration with
+AI coding agents ("harnesses") in a single Electron application.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Embedded terminals** – GPU-accelerated terminals powered by
+  [`ghostty-web`](https://github.com/jarmak-personal/ghostty-web) with a native
+  [`node-pty`](https://github.com/microsoft/node-pty) backend, split layouts,
+  and per-terminal attention badges.
+- **Git-aware workspaces** – Browse the working tree, review changes, switch
+  branches, fetch/pull, and manage worktrees from a dedicated git panel and
+  commit graph.
+- **Remote workspaces over SSH** – Open and work in projects hosted on remote
+  machines using [`ssh2`](https://github.com/mscdex/ssh2) and SSH config
+  resolution.
+- **Document review & file viewer** – View and diff files with CodeMirror,
+  Shiki syntax highlighting, Markdown (including task lists) and Mermaid
+  diagram rendering.
+- **AI harness integration** – Connect coding-agent sessions with context
+  presentation, telemetry, and document-review insertion contracts.
+- **Sessions & diagnostics** – Track sessions, workbench health, and runtime
+  diagnostics across the app.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- **Node.js** `>= 24`
+- A supported desktop platform: **macOS** or **Linux** (Debian-based packages
+  are produced for distribution)
+
+## Getting started
+
+Install dependencies. The `postinstall` step rebuilds native modules
+(`node-pty`, `@hvir/rename-noreplace`) against Electron's ABI, so a working
+native toolchain is required.
+
+```bash
+npm install
+```
+
+Run the app in development mode with hot reload:
+
+```bash
+npm run dev
+```
+
+## Building
+
+Type-check and build the production bundle:
+
+```bash
+npm run build
+```
+
+Package platform installers:
+
+```bash
+npm run pack:mac:arm64      # macOS .pkg (arm64)
+npm run pack:linux:x64      # Linux .deb (x64)
+npm run pack:linux:arm64    # Linux .deb (arm64)
+```
+
+Build output is written to `dist/`.
+
+## Development
+
+Common scripts (see `package.json` for the full list):
+
+| Command | Description |
+| --- | --- |
+| `npm run dev` | Launch the app with hot reload |
+| `npm test` | Run the unit test suite (Vitest) |
+| `npm run test:watch` | Run tests in watch mode |
+| `npm run lint` | Lint with ESLint |
+| `npm run format` | Format with Prettier |
+| `npm run typecheck` | Type-check node and web targets |
+| `npm run smoke` | Run built end-to-end smoke scenarios |
+| `npm run verify` | Full gate: seams, ADRs, architecture, lint, typecheck, tests |
+
+Install the git hooks used by the project:
+
+```bash
+npm run hooks:install
+```
+
+## Project structure
+
+```
+src/
+  main/       Electron main process (terminals, git, projects, SSH, IPC)
+  preload/    Preload bridge exposed to the renderer
+  renderer/   React UI (workbench, terminals, viewer, git, sessions)
+  shared/     Types and contracts shared across the process boundary
+  workers/    Off-main-thread workers (git, echo)
+packages/
+  rename-noreplace/  Native addon for atomic, non-clobbering renames
+scripts/      Build, packaging, smoke, and project-management tooling
+build/        Packaging resources (icons, entitlements, installer scripts)
+```
+
